  "notes": "LeFrak/Queens war-report rap on the Havoc/Marley axis. Distinguished from Mobb Deep — its nearest neighbour — by ornament rather than dread: flamenco- and Middle-Eastern-flavoured motifs over one-note ostinati, and live timbale/conga fills at the 4-bar boundaries, which nothing else on this axis carries. ⚠ `medium`, and the reason is specific: the research marks the modal specifics `[LOW-CONF]`, so `phrygian_dominant` here is the inferred parameter and the one to correct first if it sounds wrong. ⛔ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set, and it is a description rather than an exemption. The research: *\"static minor drone or i–VII; guitar/oud-style plucks and low strings carry the hook\"*. The ostinato states it. ⚠ `chordDurationBeats` carries this model's chord variety rather than more progressions. Its harmony is one or two chords by description, and `melodic_variety.rs` still requires the generated chord part to reach 55 distinct outputs — so what varies is how long the loop sits on a chord, not what the chord is. Adding families it does not play would have been the dishonest fix. ⚠ The i–VI family is INFERRED, not researched — the research names only the static form. It carries a low weight and exists because the generated chord part still owes a producer 55 distinct outputs over 200 seeds; it is the first thing to delete if this model ever sounds busier than the records do.",
